From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Forward Python_INCLUDE_DIR to the nested project

The real target is an ExternalProject whose CMAKE_CACHE_ARGS list forwards only
the TRITON_* options and a few CMAKE_* ones. An OE build sets Python_INCLUDE_DIR
to the target headers on the top-level command line, and without forwarding it
the nested FindPython takes /usr/include/python3.14 from the build host, which the
cross toolchain rejects.

The argument is added only when the variable is set, so a build that does not set
it behaves as before.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-Specific]
Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
---
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -179,6 +179,13 @@
   set(TRITON_DEPENDS ${TRITON_DEPENDS} opentelemetry-cpp)
 endif() # TRITON_ENABLE_TRACING
 
+# OE cross builds pass the target headers' directory; without it FindPython in the
+# nested project takes the include path from the build host's interpreter.
+set(TRITON_PYTHON_ARGS)
+if(Python_INCLUDE_DIR)
+  set(TRITON_PYTHON_ARGS -DPython_INCLUDE_DIR:PATH=${Python_INCLUDE_DIR})
+endif()
+
 ExternalProject_Add(triton-server
   PREFIX triton-server
   SOURCE_DIR "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src"
@@ -211,4 +218,5 @@
     -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX:PATH=${TRITON_INSTALL_PREFIX}
     -DTRITON_VERSION:STRING=${TRITON_VERSION}
     -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH:PATH=${CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH}
+    ${TRITON_PYTHON_ARGS}
 )
